    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">\n\n\n\t\n\t\n\t\n\t\n\n\n<p style=\"line-height:100%\">Hi :) I am working on a salamander\nmorphology project and have very little experience working with\ncomputer software and coding. Using tpsUtil32, we converted our\nimages to TPS files, appended the files into a master TPS file, and\nthen plotted 12 landmarks on each image in tpsDig232. Then we entered\nthese commands in Geomorph: \n</p>\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0in;border:none;padding:0in;line-height:100%\">\n<font color=\"#0000ff\"><font face=\"Ubuntu Mono\"><font style=\"font-size:10pt\" size=\"2\">readland.tps(file.choose())</font></font></font></p>\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0in;border:none;padding:0in;line-height:100%\">\n<font color=\"#0000ff\"><font face=\"Ubuntu Mono\"><font style=\"font-size:10pt\" size=\"2\">MyShapeData_tps=readland.tps(</font></font></font></p>\n<pre style=\"border:none;padding:0in;line-height:100%\"><a name=\"m_4440130336561449022_m_-7499447185044495357_rstudio_console_output\" rel=\"nofollow\"></a><font color=\"#0000ff\"><font face=\"Ubuntu Mono\"><font style=\"font-size:10pt\" size=\"2\">fixed.angle(myShapeData_tps,<a href=\"http://art.pt/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://art.pt/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792485177107000&amp;usg=AOvVaw21Nuz1jkKrb9cIu0dLDZOK\">art.pt</a>=1,angle.pts=c(5,6),rot.pts=c(2,3,4,5))</font></font></font>\n<a name=\"m_4440130336561449022_m_-7499447185044495357_rstudio_console_output1\" rel=\"nofollow\"></a><font color=\"#0000ff\"><font face=\"Ubuntu Mono\"><font style=\"font-size:10pt\" size=\"2\">myData.super &lt;- gpagen(myShapeData_tps)</font></font></font>\n<a name=\"m_4440130336561449022_m_-7499447185044495357_rstudio_console_output2\" rel=\"nofollow\"></a><font color=\"#0000ff\"><font face=\"Ubuntu Mono\"><font style=\"font-size:10pt\" size=\"2\">plotTangentSpace(fixed.angle(myShapeData_tps,<a href=\"http://art.pt/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://art.pt/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792485177107000&amp;usg=AOvVaw21Nuz1jkKrb9cIu0dLDZOK\">art.pt</a>=1,angle.pts=c(5,6),rot.pts=c(2,3,4,5)))</font></font></font></pre><p style=\"line-height:100%\">\nOur main question is: how do you correctly code for superimposition?\nWe attempted entering <font color=\"#0000ff\"><font face=\"Ubuntu Mono\"><font style=\"font-size:10pt\" size=\"2\">myData.super\n&lt;- gpagen(myShapeData_tps) </font></font></font>but this\nconsistently seemed to do nothing. A line appeared on the screen\nlabeled 100%, but our resulting plot looked the same regardless of\nwhether we used the command or not. We appreciate any help you can\nprovide!</p><p style=\"line-height:100%\">Thanks,</p><p style=\"line-height:100%\">Brittany<br></p>\n\n</div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "g3kZtXSEFgAJ",
   "from": "Adams, Dean [EEOBS]",
