   "subject": "RE: [geomorph-r-package] Geomorph Superimposition",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div lang=\"EN-US\" link=\"blue\" vlink=\"purple\">\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\">Brittany,<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\">In your code you performed a GPA superimposition, and placed the output in ‘</span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Ubuntu Mono&quot;,serif;color:blue\">myData.super</span><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\">’. \r\n But then, your plot of specimens using plotTangentSpace called your original data, not the superimposed data.\r\n<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\">A more careful reading of the help files of geomorph, and some additional familiarity with R, will assist in these issues. I suggest you begin there. Geomorph’s\r\n help files are rather extensive and laden with many examples: including for what you are attempting to do.\r\n<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\">Dean<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\">Dr. Dean C. Adams<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\">Director of Graduate Education, EEB Program<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\">Professor<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\">Department of Ecology, Evolution, and Organismal Biology<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\">Iowa State University<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><a href=\"https://www.eeob.iastate.edu/faculty/adams/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.eeob.iastate.edu/faculty/adams/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792485177109000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1DskrwsckYgQm4vmkbKQ_6\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\">https://www.eeob.iastate.edu/faculty/adams/</span></a><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\"><u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\">phone: <a href=\"tel:(515)%20294-3834\" value=\"+15152943834\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\">515-294-3834</a><u></u><u></u></span></p></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div lang=\"EN-US\" link=\"blue\" vlink=\"purple\"><div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><b><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\">From:</span></b><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\"> <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">geomorph-...@googlegroups.com</a> &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">geomorph-...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt;\r\n<b>On Behalf Of </b><a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">bashea...@st.nashcc.edu</a><br>\r\n<b>Sent:</b> Friday, January 25, 2019 12:21 PM<br>\r\n<b>To:</b> geomorph R package &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">geomorph-...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt;<br>\r\n<b>Subject:</b> [geomorph-r-package] Geomorph Superimposition<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<div>\r\n<p>Hi :) I am working on a salamander morphology project and have very little experience working with computer software and coding. Using tpsUtil32, we converted our images to TPS files, appended the files into a master TPS file, and then plotted 12 landmarks\r\n on each image in tpsDig232. Then we entered these commands in Geomorph: <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Ubuntu Mono&quot;,serif;color:blue\">readland.tps(file.choose())</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Ubuntu Mono&quot;,serif;color:blue\">MyShapeData_tps=readland.tps(</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<pre><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Ubuntu Mono&quot;,serif;color:blue\">fixed.angle(myShapeData_tps,</span><a href=\"http://art.pt/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://art.pt/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792485177109000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2iQHqzG01zwHyWOvWqq11V\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Ubuntu Mono&quot;,serif\">art.pt</span></a><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Ubuntu Mono&quot;,serif;color:blue\">=1,angle.pts=c(5,6),rot.pts=c(2,3,4,5))</span><u></u><u></u></pre>\r\n<pre><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Ubuntu Mono&quot;,serif;color:blue\">myData.super &lt;- gpagen(myShapeData_tps)</span><u></u><u></u></pre>\r\n<pre><a name=\"m_9105753170194794772_m_-7499447185044495357_rstudio_console_o\" rel=\"nofollow\"></a><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Ubuntu Mono&quot;,serif;color:blue\">plotTangentSpace(fixed.angle(myShapeData_tps,</span><a href=\"http://art.pt/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://art.pt/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792485177109000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2iQHqzG01zwHyWOvWqq11V\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Ubuntu Mono&quot;,serif\">art.pt</span></a><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Ubuntu Mono&quot;,serif;color:blue\">=1,angle.pts=c(5,6),rot.pts=c(2,3,4,5)))</span><u></u><u></u></pre>\r\n<p>Our main question is: how do you correctly code for superimposition? We attempted entering\r\n<span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Ubuntu Mono&quot;,serif;color:blue\">\r\nmyData.super &lt;- gpagen(myShapeData_tps) </span>but this consistently seemed to do nothing. A line appeared on the screen labeled 100%, but our resulting plot looked the same regardless of whether we used the command or not. We appreciate any help you can provide!<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p>Thanks,<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p>Brittany<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div></div>"
